# Causeway — project rules

Causeway answers "why did <metric> change?" for small businesses by testing rival hypotheses against
real data federated through Zetaris, and shows the evidence behind every sentence.

- TypeScript on Node 22, ESM, strict mode. Fastify API on :8000, Vite React UI on :8080.
- **Models propose, code decides.** No model ever writes SQL, computes a statistic or issues a verdict.
  SQL comes only from `src/tests/compiler.ts` templates; statistics only from `src/stats/`; verdicts only
  from the rule table in `src/stats/rules.ts`.
- **Portable SQL subset only** (valid in Zetaris Lightning / Spark SQL and DuckDB): SELECT, JOIN, GROUP BY,
  window functions, CASE, CAST, simple arithmetic. One statement per call, no trailing semicolon.
- Every model call goes through `src/meterless/generator.ts` (the Meterless-style injected generator).
- Meterless engines under `vendor/meterless/` are vendored unmodified; adapt them in `src/meterless/`.
- Never invent data. Synthetic business ledgers are labelled synthetic everywhere. Never read
  `bench/truth/` or `output_examples/` from `src/`.
- Every agent action writes a JSONL trace line (`logs/trace-<run>.jsonl`).
- English only in code, comments, UI and docs.
